#------ Input file for system specifications

# USER: 
#    1) The information within this file is meant to allow for the most efficient program run, meaning accurate information is important
#    2) The filesystem stripe size is only required on an HPC system. Otherwise, if turned on when on a personal computer, there is no
#       guarantee that the most optimal times will occur.
#       It is highly recommended to research how to obtain your computers filesystem stripe size
#       
#       Common filesystem environments and their commands:
#       1) Lustre: lfs getstripe <file/directory>
#       2) IBM Spectrum Scale (GPFS): mmlsfs <file> -B
#       3) BeeGFS: beegfs-ctl --getentryinfo <file/directory>
#       
#       If the HPC you are using is not above, please research how to get the filesystem stripe size (which may not be called "stripe" size
#       depending on the filesystem).
#
#       NOTE: You should be able to use the command `df -T <file>` or `mount | grep <file>` to figure out the filesystem being used.
#
# NOTE: This file follows a key-value pair. That is, the value is only matched with the key
# eliminating the possibility of incorrect reads due to line dependencies.

FileSystemStripeSize 0    // Amount of memory written to an OST before moving onto the next (HPC/supercomputers only), 0 = off (kilobytes)
AvailableMem         8    // Amount of memory (RAM) allocated to the process (gigabytes)
